# Firestore Launch Reminder

Before production launch or any deployment/release checklist, remind the user to tighten Firestore `activities` update rules.

Current MVP rules may allow any signed-in user to update `activities`. Before launch, restrict updates to only the fields needed for reservation, such as `currentPlayers`, `participantUids`, `participants`, and `updatedAt`, and validate that the update cannot oversell or edit host-owned activity details.
